ile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks as typed operation artifacts, not whole-component completion. Preserve every source facet and unresolved metadata ID in the exact phase-09 decision allocation; no implementation acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/runtime/ai-memory-policy: At the selected AI memory/retrieval provider enforce source/trust/tenant namespace, schema and sink-taint policy, privacy, retention, deletion and embedding/provider identity. Emit memory read/write/retrieval/deletion decisions and replay identity; accept validated authorized access, reject cross-namespace/ungranted writes, expired retention, forbidden secret storage and unvalidated retrieved content at trusted sinks. Provider billing/account constraints remain external; project accounting cannot become an admission condition. Decision criterion interface/runtime/durable-effect-replay: Execute durable steps against versioned recorded inputs/outputs with workflow/step/event/effect/provider identity, idempotency and declared completion/transaction boundaries. Recorded-output segments consume matching records without reissuing external actions, rejecting missing/mismatched/order-inconsistent records; preserve retries, cancellation and compensation policy. R6 graph-declared replay-safe repetitions may execute only where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies and authority still holds. Emit restart/replay equality and actual no-duplicate-effect traces; a replay-safe label cannot override required recorded behavior. Decision criterion interface/runtime/model-provider-execution: Invoke the declared model/provider through its typed prompt/message provenance, roles/digests, parameters/decoding settings, output schema and validation policy, preserving input taint, output validation, errors, source identity and replay/audit mode. Record actual provider/model substitution only when policy permits it. Accept an authorized validated response and reject wrong provider/model/decoding identity, prohibited substitution, missing validation/grant or live invocation in a required recorded-output segment; retain external billing policy without compiler work quotas. Decision criterion interface/runtime/nondeterminism-recording: For each admitted runtime action whose replay or audit policy requires recording, persist typed input/output digests, provider/action identity, error/retry decisions, timestamp source and source/generated origin; record scheduler decisions where replay depends on them. Emit actual record-mode traces and matching replay consumption, rejecting absent/mismatched identity/order/cardinality and silent live reexecution in recorded-output mode. Record-mode action and replay-mode consumption are conditional alternatives, not simultaneous mandatory effects; retain R6's authorized graph-declared repetition exception outside R7/R8 recorded-output obligations. Decision criterion interface/runtime/replay-compatible-upgrade: For a code/topology/schema or workflow-version upgrade, compare existing event histories, persisted state, actor snapshots and message versions against the new declared compatibility/migration/replay policy. Emit migration and replay evidence that existing histories remain usable; reject incompatible upgrades without such policy/evidence, schemaless state/messages and implicit rewriting of recorded external outcomes. Preserve idempotency, retry/cancellation/compensation and authority semantics across the admitted upgrade. Decision criterion interface/runtime/tool-provider-execution: Invoke the declared tool/provider with input/output schemas and validation, effect/side-effect class, caller grant intersected with the tool's own contract, timeout/retry/error mapping and required review/secret/taint policy. Emit actual invocation and policy/review decision records with replay identity; reject ungranted or out-of-contract effects, missing required review, invalid/tainted sink values, secret-policy violations and live calls 