dators/codecs and parity artifacts; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-is-not-host-semantics: Normalize an admitted foreign value/failure/callback through its declared typed and audited Gravity boundary while preserving Gravity errors, source identity, effects and capability requirements. Refusals: Reject a host null, exception, reflection/loading convention or object-identity assumption leaking into portable Gravity semantics; keep actual adaptation separate from manifest publication. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/typed-object-boundary (Open): Input: Host object boundary with runtime/version, symbol/class/module/member, Gravity/host type, rooting/ownership/lifetime, exception translation, affinity, effects/grants and source-map support. Accept: Emit and validate typed schema/protocol/foreign-handle boundaries before manipulation; insufficient metadata yields opaque values operated only through declared provider APIs. Reject: Untyped host object use, missing lifecycle/affinity/grant metadata and unnormalized host failures crossing into Gravity. Required outputs: Host interop/object/runtime dependency and deployment-capability manifests, typed-versus-opaque boundary fixtures, P4-HOST-OBJECT/EXCEPTION/CROSS-IMPORT and effect/grant diagnostics. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, schema, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/typed-object-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/native/ffi-boundary (Open): Input: Native foreign import/call with ABI/calling convention, link symbol, type mapping, ownership transfer/lifetime/nullability, failure/affinity, effects/grants and safe-wrapper or unsafe contract. Accept: Validate the complete foreign boundary, execute the admitted call through the wrapper, and separately translate declared foreign failures into Gravity; preserve ABI/source/provider identity and every safe-wrapper precondition. Reject: Raw import called directly from safe code, incomplete ABI/ownership/error metadata, missing grant, invalid lifetime/nullability/affinity and untranslated failure or unaudited raw memory. Required outputs: Native ABI/FFI/safety manifests and admitted/rejected call/failure fixtures with P5-FFI/RAW-MEMORY diagnostics identifying ABI/provider/effect/grant/source/generated origin. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping native/ffi-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Source obligation `language/concurrency/execute-owned-actor-message`: Execute typed/effect-visible actor messages against actor-owned state, preserving scheduler/failure assumptions and explicit durable schema/replay boundaries. Accept: Execute typed, effect-visible messages against actor-owned state with explicit capability requirements, scheduler assumptions and failure behavior. A durable actor/service boundary carries schema/artifact identity and replay records. Reject: Reject state access outside actor ownership, untyped or undeclared-effect messages, missing required grants and durable delivery without schema/replay evidence. Required outputs: Actor state/message schemas, scheduler/failure manifest, ownership/effect/grant decisions and durable replay/denial traces. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-async-suspension`: Interpret typed async suspend/await operations with scheduler wakeup, cancellation and timeout behavior admitted by the active profile. Accept: Interpret typed async suspend/await, scheduler wakeup, cancellation and timeout operations only for a profile/runtime supporting the handler and resume mode; preserve handler identity, original labels, residual effects and required grants. Reject: Reject request/response/result mismatch, unsupported scheduler/profile, missing authority, resume after cancel/completion or illegal captured lifetime. Required outputs: Typed handler/runtime contract, suspend/wakeup/await/cancel/timeout traces, cleanup records and stable rejection diagnostics. Dependencies 