n host/foreign type identity, ownership transfer on failure, cleanup, abort policy, runtime dependencies and exception/null contracts for hosted dispatch. Reject: Reject an unexpected or undeclared null, null crossing a non-null type, untranslated/untyped foreign failure and a missing mapping or failure-resource contract; report P4-EXCEPTION, L8-HOST-DISPATCH, L9-HOST-ERROR/L9-FFI-ERROR or L19-ERROR-MAP as applicable. Required outputs: Foreign/host dispatch and error-mapping artifacts, hosted conformance, failure-cleanup tests and diagnostics with host/runtime, source/generated origin, requested effect, grant, symbol and deployment policy when relevant. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/memory/release-provider-storage`: Release or transfer a provider-managed/foreign/linear allocation according to lifetime, finalization and matching allocator identity, rejecting leaks, double release and incompatible release operations. Accept: Release or transfer provider/foreign/linear storage under declared destruction/finalization and exactly-once rules. Match allocator identity with a compatible release operation; preserve transfer direction, borrowed lifetime, nullability, initialization, errors, thread affinity and callback lifetime. Unexpressible foreign facts require an unsafe boundary or checked wrapper. Reject: Reject leaks, double release, incompatible allocator/releaser and a safe binding missing ownership/lifetime/nullability/allocator facts; report L18-LEAK, L18-DOUBLE-RELEASE or L18-FFI-ALLOCATOR. Required outputs: Provider/foreign allocation-release and ownership records, leak/exactly-once/allocator-mismatch fixtures, checked-wrapper or unsafe-policy evidence and diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Decision criterion `interface/runtime/check-allocation-provider-policy` (Open): Before selecting or using an allocation provider, check that its family, effects, layout/alignment, lifetime, failure and release contract satisfies the namespace/profile/target memory policy. Refuse: Reject wrong provider family, undeclared effects, incompatible layout/lifetime/failure or release behavior before allocation; this is a semantic provider check, not a compiler work allowance. Required outputs: allocation-provider selection/admission manifest and compatibility/failure/release refusal fixtures. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks as typed operation artifacts, not whole-component completion. Preserve every source facet and unresolved metadata ID in the exact phase-09 decision allocation; no implementation acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/runtime/concurrency-memory-order: For every selected atomic/lock/thread/scheduler provider execute the declared operation, memory order, synchronization scope, alignment and target support under accepted race/ownership evidence. Emit operation/provider/target records and synchronization/transfer traces; accept representable supported synchronization and reject unsupported orders/scopes, misalignment, unprotected shared mutation and undeclared host-thread fallback. Compile-time race evidence remains required independen